spec.section:
## K.10 Required evidence checklist

A reviewer may mark a report/objective accepted only after reading back:

- resolved `request_ref`, matching send/attempt/session and harness timestamps;
- selected content class, schema version/digest, validation result and immutable content ref;
- every criterion's provenance/version, verdict and non-empty evidence refs;
- dataset atomic publication state and complete row/query readback, or explicit partial state;
- child review verdicts before parent roll-up;
- wait state and resolution evidence, if applicable;
- delivery evidence and reused idempotency key, if delivery is required;
- explicit distinctions among attempt closure, human gate, resumed execution, objective acceptance
  and delivery.

No fresh timestamp, successful transport, approval, green counter, or status label can replace
this evidence ladder.


**CHD-3.3 contract:** `tables/section11-lifecycle-source.json` is the single Section 11 state source. `tables/section11-transition-table.csv`, `tables/section11-ladder.csv`, all Section 11 schemas and `examples/reports/section11-lifecycle.json` are checked companions generated or validated from that source; `contracts/request-attempt-lifecycle.md` is the explanatory contract. `tables/verify-ladder.csv` remains the legacy compatibility projection and must not define a second ladder.
